CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ two elements: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ empty: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ converting constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
apply_default_template_arguments took the pack's size from the function
parameter pack expansion only (pack_expansion_size); for a pack deduced
from a parameter type it now uses the elements recorded in pack_args_map.
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
